_ref_lock_push.py while acquire/_cas_advance/release remain in _ref_lock.py, so _ref_lock.py becomes a consumer of the sibling — a parent->child call edge the 'pass core down' narrative does not address"],"finding":"The plan enumerates the split-out symbols' consumers as only 'the one test', but _push_cas and _push_delete_cas have internal callers that STAY in _ref_lock.py (acquire at line 393, _cas_advance at line 476, release at line 422) — the plan's seam design only describes passing `core` down to the child, not how the parent _ref_lock.py reaches back into _ref_lock_push.py to invoke the moved _push_cas/_push_delete_cas.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f10db1c355a5eda84","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Seam section: 'Nothing outside `_ref_lock.py` references these names except the one test above.'","norm_id":"nee512197ccafb288","priority":0.85,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["After the move, acquire()/release()/_cas_advance() in _ref_lock.py still call _push_cas/_push_delete_cas which now live in the sibling; without a way for _ref_lock.py to obtain the moved functions (a lazy_load import of _ref_lock_push, or leaving thin wrappers behind), remote-path acquire/release break at runtime with NameError."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend the 'resolvable at the original path' guarantee to `_push_cas` and `_push_delete_cas` too: keep 4-arg wrappers of both bound in `_ref_lock` (injecting `core=sys.modules[__name__]`) so the in-module callers at lines 393, 422 and 476 keep working without a prohibited cross-module import.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.25,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["`_push_cas` is invoked inside `_ref_lock.py` at line 393 (`_push_cas(repo_root, ref, oid, _ZERO_OID, remote)` in the acquire `_plant` closure) and line 476 (advance `_do` closure), both bare 4-arg calls with no `core`.","`_push_delete_cas` is invoked inside `_ref_lock.py` at line 422 (`_push_delete_cas(repo_root, ref, oid, remote)`).","The plan's cluster list includes `_push_cas` and `_push_delete_cas` as MOVED, but the 'resolvable at the original path' guarantee is stated only for `_push_lease_cas`.","Trap 1 forbids `from rebar._engine.rebar_reconciler.X import ...`, so the moved child functions cannot simply be imported back into these call sites."],"finding":"The plan moves `_push_cas` and `_push_delete_cas` into `_ref_lock_push.py` but only requires `_push_lease_cas` to stay resolvable (with a wrapper) at the original `_ref_lock` path; the in-module production callers of `_push_cas`/`_push_delete_cas` are not accounted for, so the mechanism as specified breaks those call sites.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6ef2bcdbcec31f9d","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Seam section: 'keep _ref_lock._push_lease_cas (with its current 5-argument signature) resolvable at the original path'","norm_id":"n449e6c4540c5f142","priority":0.85,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["Production acquire path (`_plant`) with a non-None remote calls `_push_cas` and raises NameError, or is silently rewired to call the child module's `_push_cas(core, ...)` with a wrong signature.","Release/advance paths (`_do`, delete) similarly break."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In `_ref_lock.py`, after `lazy_load`ing the child, bind thin wrappers for all three moved entry points, e.g. `def _push_cas(repo_root, ref, new_oid, old_oid, remote): return _push_mod._push_cas(sys.modules[__name__], repo_root, ref, new_oid, old_oid, remote)` (and likewise `_push_delete_cas`, `_push_lease_cas`), so the original call sites at 393/422/476 are unchanged.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend the seam so _ref_lock.py re-resolves _push_cas and _push_delete_cas (called at :393, :476, :422) from the moved sibling — specify the lazy_load/import path back into _ref_lock.py, not only the child->paren